     I've been seeing a lot of talk about making the game harder, and
modifications to various parts of the game and I have some comments and
questions along this line . Why is it that monsters are always
attacking?  Do I appeard terrifying to them?  Can they sense my
alignment? if so then why is it the same regardless of my alignment?

     Someone mentioned monsters being able to scratch Elbereth.  I think
i've also seen suggestions to allow monsters to purchase & sell items to
wandering merchants.  (Gypsys perhaps?).  I've noticed that certain
Orc's attack in packs.  And were-beasties can call on their bretheren
for help.

     The fact that these actions are programmed into the game seems to
imply that players want the beasties/opponents in the game to have some
personality - to appear to be making _individual_ decisions to attack or
not rather than simply attacking because everyone else is doing so.  Why
not have a beastie be terrified by the player's imposing figure... and
run screaming from the room to hide from you.  -- you hear manic
screaming in the distance --.  Also, some rare individual monster might
be a berserker and absolutely go nuts attacking you.  Why can't the
monsters pray to _their_ god for healing?

     Do the monsters have any life other than to hang around and wait
for you? to kill or be killed?  There are shades of this with the Nurse,
Nymph, Rockmoles, Dwarves, Gnomes... possibly others, but only shades.
Why are the majority of the creatures encountered _male_.  Wouldn't some
of the beasties cultures have female warriors/priests/store keepers?

     What is the prupose of all these rooms on each level?  They're
almost always empty - totally contrary to our own culture.  You're
dealing with over 50 cultures in the game-world, all of them living in
harmony, requiring no personal items other than weapons and goodies.
Why don't they have houses down there where their familes are?  Instead
of that door on the edge of the screen leading to a closet, it could
open into a personal/group dwelling - cooking, sleeping, family areas.


     Why do I drown when I fall in the water?  I can swim...  I can dive
too.  Why not add a whole new plane to the adventure? let an underground
river flow through certain levels (perhaps connecting them?)... you can
go fishing, do swimming... you have to cross rickity old bridges to get
to other parts of the level.  Maybe trolls live under them demanding
fare to pass?  What if you fall in?  Hold your breath, drop whatever you
can live without and let the current carry you until you hit a shallow
area (on another level).

-- you find blessed divers tanks --

What kinds of passages/adventures can one find underwater?

enjoy,
-Garet
                                                                                        


